## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

**This is a textbook coverage-touching suite.** All 10 production methods are called — giving you 95% line coverage — but almost nothing is actually verified. This explains exactly why bugs escape to production.

| Severity | Count |
|----------|-------|
| 🔴 Critical | 6 |
| 🟠 High | 1 |
| 🟡 Medium | 2 |
| Total | **9** |

---

### 🔴 Critical Findings

#### 1. Coverage-Touching Pattern (systemic)
**Location:** Entire test class (lines 6–89)

The suite methodically calls every public method on `ProductCatalog` in declaration order with zero or trivial assertions. **6 of 10 tests have no assertion at all**, and the remaining 4 use only `Assert.IsNotNull` — a near-meaningless check on non-nullable return types.

This is the single root cause of your production bugs: the tests exercise code paths for coverage metrics but never verify behavior.

---

#### 2. No Assertions — `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)
Calls `AddProduct` but never checks the product was stored.

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_StoresProduct()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);

    var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved?.Name);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved?.Price);
}
```

#### 3. No Assertions — `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 32)
Calls `UpdatePrice` but never checks the price actually changed.

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void UpdatePrice_ChangesPriceOfExistingProduct()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);

    var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated?.Price);
}
```

#### 4. No Assertions — `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 39)
Calls `RemoveProduct` but never verifies the product is gone.

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void RemoveProduct_DeletesProductFromCatalog()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");

    Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
}
```

#### 5. No Assertions — `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63)
Calls `GetProductCount` but discards the result entirely.

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetProductCount_ReturnsNumberOfProducts()
{
